  "title": "Dataset of an EEG-based BCI experiment in Virtual Reality using P300",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 21 healthy participants performing a visual P300 brain-computer interface speller task in two conditions: on a personal computer and in virtual reality with a passive smartphone-based head-mounted display. The study compares physiological, subjective and performance aspects of P300-based BCI across the two platforms. Data were recorded with 16 wet electrodes at 512 Hz at GIPSA-lab in 2018.",
  "methods_description": "Two randomized sessions (PC and VR) per participant, each with 12 blocks of 5 repetitions. In each repetition, 12 groups of 6 symbols flashed in a 6x6 matrix, with each symbol flashing exactly twice. Stimuli were produced with the Unity engine. EEG was recorded with a g.USBamp amplifier (16 electrodes, 10-10 montage, right earlobe reference, AFZ ground) and OpenViBE software. Random feedback was given after each repetition.",
